// The Observatory (Observatory_2; character-bibles.md §1). The Return: Pell holds the frame's door while Wren
// chooses. Pell's last list is one item long, and it is whatever voice Wren has used most (Voices.Dominant):
// Surveyor, "the leaves"; Warden, "her"; Drift, "the sky". The choice itself is NAR-13's.

title: Observatory_Pell_Return
---
<<if not has_flag("act3.started")>>
    Pell: The dome's shut. Which, technically, means we're not meant to be up here. Again. #line:002dd4b
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("pell.last_list")>>
    Pell: I'm holding the door. Go on. #still #line:086f924
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pell: One thing. Just one. I've been practising. #line:0ec7147
<<if dominant_voice() == "warden">>
    Pell: Her. Whoever she is, the one you're doing this for. Her. #line:05f5401
    <<flag pell.last_list 2>>
<<elseif dominant_voice() == "drift">>
    Pell: The sky. That's the list. It's a short list. It's a big item. #line:0e57e5d
    <<flag pell.last_list 3>>
<<else>>
    Pell: The leaves. The ones in the orchard that fall. Keep those. #line:0f2026d
    <<flag pell.last_list 1>>
<<endif>>
Pell: That's it. That's the whole list. Go on. I'll hold the door. #line:02c49ad
===
